    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Twenty-two years after Maxwell&#x27;s equations predicted electromagnetic radiation, Heinrich Hertz built an oscillating dipole antenna -- an induction coil driving a spark gap -- and detected the resulting waves meters away, confirming they travel at the speed of light and can be reflected, refracted, and polarized just like ordinary light. On the 2D Yee grid used here, the out-of-plane field E_z and the in-plane fields H_x, H_y obey the source-free TMz-mode reduction of Maxwell&#x27;s curl equations,">

